../../guards/guard-measured-fit.md:7:1. **A measurement row exists, with provenance.** The item's build record contains a fit table with one row per subject text element: element id · container (box/strip/line) · the INSTRUMENT (harness run or rendered-measurement tool that produced the row) · the fitted element + stage geometry · MEASURED ink bounds after fitting (glyph ink height and width, from post-fit measurement of the rendered geometry at the 360 px stage) · container bounds · margin on the binding side. A text element with no row, or a row missing its measurement provenance, is a HIT. *(Provenance form added 2026-11-18, recreation Cycle 035 Condense — Amendment A12's paired landing: T196 + T197's model rows.)*
