    18	- ONE stream: this instruction + the technique's packet section + TECHNIQUES.md entry + prior scores.md/verdict-history lines for the technique and family siblings — never pipe + stdin together (fleet rule; a doubled stream voids the run).
    19	- Fires per item at §1 step 1, before the mechanics summary is written — every item, including items with no prior attempt (the audit then prices the packet section's internal consistency as its finding).
    20	- **Cycle-level form (amendment, 2026-11-14, Cycle 009 Condense — from that cycle's codex-observe set-aside):** in a wave with zero items the audit fires ONCE on the pool record (QUEUE section · TECHNIQUES register · INDEX state · verdict-history · artifact census). The packet fed to a cycle-level audit MUST carry the seat's binding census (per-directory codex/ return presence + the per-attempt binding basis) — an excerpts-only packet prices as an audit of excerpts, the feeder records the packet's limitation in the cycle record, and the auditor remains free to return NOT-CONFIRMED whenever the supplied evidence, census included, is insufficient (the requirement binds the feeder's packet, never the auditor's verdict). Every record line the census references without reproducing (no-verdict lines, status-lag rows, hand-off entries) is identified in the packet by subject + disposition — a referenced-but-unidentified line prices as a gap in the audit (amendment, 2026-11-15, Cycle 010: the fed census counted verdict-history's no-verdict line without identifying it; codex-observe's CONFIRMED-WITH-GAPS named the omission). First demonstration: Cycle 009 Wave 7 (return filed in that run directory; set-aside + miss recorded there).
    21	- **Sequencing rule (amendment, 2026-11-15, Cycle 011 Condense — from deviation D1, priced as an escape by that cycle's codex-condense REVISE):** in a cycle-level firing, the seat files this call's return in the run directory BEFORE the jev-observe-exit judge for the same cycle is started, and the filed return is provided to that judge as part of its record. If the return is unavailable when the judge must start, the missing receipt is recorded explicitly in the run record (never silently absent). Founding incident: Cycle 011 Wave 9 — the seat filed the return while the judge was already running; the judge priced the absence as its Gap G4 and Plan had to cure it by receipt (RUN.md §2 P4, that cycle).
